ASTM D6673 Apparel DXF Compliance – Technical Appendix
Project Summary

This appendix documents how the skirt and waistband patterns comply with ASTM D6673 (DXF-ASTM) requirements for apparel exchange, including geometry conventions, layer semantics, tuck representation, notching, grading, and interoperability expectations with Gerber and Lectra systems.

Pattern Pieces

Skirt – Front (Cut 3)

Skirt – Back (Cut 3)

Waistband (Cut 2)

Units & DXF Profile

Units: Inches

DXF: ASCII, AutoCAD R13-compatible

Entities: LINE, TEXT only (no proprietary objects)

Layer Semantics (ASTM-Style)

CUT: Final cut edge (includes seam allowance and hem allowance)

SEAM: Stitching/seam lines

FOLD: Fold lines (tucks, hem fold)

STITCH: Tuck stitch lines

NOTCH: Notches

GRAIN: Grainline

TEXT: Construction notes

Tuck Specification

Total tucks per piece: 10

Center inverted box tuck: 1 (counts as 2 tucks)

Stitch on CF/CB

Fold lines at ±1.8"

Knife tucks: 8

Centers every 1.9"

Fold offset 1.8"

Tuck length: 6.0"

Press direction:

Front: Knife tucks pressed toward CF; box tuck pressed inward

Back: Knife tucks pressed toward CB; box tuck pressed inward

Notching Scheme

Double notch at CF/CB for center box tuck

Single notch at each knife tuck stitch location

Hip alignment notch on side seams

Center hem reference notch

Seam Allowances & Hem

Seam allowance: 0.5"

Hem allowance: 2.0"

Hem fold line: 0.5" above hem

Grading (ASTM Style)

Base size: as drafted

Linear grade applied at waist, hip, and hem

Tucks retain depth (1.8"); spacing adjusts proportionally

Grade increments documented separately (see Grading Table)

Interoperability Expectations
Gerber AccuMark

Reads R13 ASCII DXF

Honors layer-based semantics

Tucks interpreted from FOLD/STITCH geometry

Lectra Modaris

Accepts ASTM DXF with explicit geometry

Notches imported as cut symbols

Text imported as annotations

Compliance Statement

This pattern adheres to ASTM D6673 requirements by using explicit, non-proprietary DXF entities, standardized layer usage, and redundant physical indicators (folds, stitches, notches, and text). The file is suitable for exchange, review, and production in major apparel CAD systems.

Prepared for Grant Submission

This appendix may be included verbatim as a technical compliance exhibit accompanying funding or program proposals.